From: da-ai-xian-zun <163512031+da-ai-xian-zun@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:07:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] qcomtee: raise MAX_OUTBOUND_BUFFER_SIZE from 4K to 1M

The Goodix fingerprint TA returns large responses (device info about
5.5 KB, interrupt payloads around 320 KB); QTEE rejects a too-small
outbound buffer with OBJECT_ERROR_MAXDATA. 1M stays within an order-8
alloc_pages_exact() allocation and needs no CMA.
---
 drivers/tee/qcomtee/shm.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tee/qcomtee/shm.c b/drivers/tee/qcomtee/shm.c
index 26b2ce699..e8dea394e 100644
--- a/drivers/tee/qcomtee/shm.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/qcomtee/shm.c
@@ -15,9 +15,13 @@
 /**
  * define MAX_OUTBOUND_BUFFER_SIZE - Maximum size of outbound buffers.
  *
- * The size of outbound buffer depends on QTEE callback requests.
+ * The size of outbound buffer depends on QTEE callback requests. Raised from
+ * SZ_4K to SZ_1M: Goodix goodixfp64 TA responses are large (GET_DEV_INFO ~5.5KB,
+ * IRQ event payload ~320KB; reqOut+rspOut for IRQ ~655KB). QTEE rejects an
+ * invoke whose outbound buffer is too small with OBJECT_ERROR_MAXDATA (-95).
+ * 1MB stays within alloc_pages_exact() order-8 (no CMA needed).
  */
-#define MAX_OUTBOUND_BUFFER_SIZE SZ_4K
+#define MAX_OUTBOUND_BUFFER_SIZE SZ_1M
 
 /**
  * define MAX_INBOUND_BUFFER_SIZE - Maximum size of the inbound buffer.
